@startuml WF-04_Robot_Human_Handoff
title WF-04: Robot-to-Human Handoff (Feature F-04 | Scenarios DS-07, DS-08)\nProject: Intelligent Hotel Concierge Robot (HC-Robot) - FA26SE905 | Baseline: review-2

skinparam monochrome false
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam defaultFontName "Segoe UI"
skinparam defaultFontSize 12
skinparam ActivityBackgroundColor #F8FAFC
skinparam ActivityBorderColor #334155
skinparam ActivityDiamondBackgroundColor #FEF3C7
skinparam ActivityDiamondBorderColor #D97706
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor #EFF6FF
skinparam NoteBorderColor #3B82F6
skinparam SwimlaneTitleFontSize 13
skinparam SwimlaneBorderColor #64748B

|Hotel Guest|
start
:Interact with Concierge Robot during active AI session;

|Concierge Robot|
:Maintain AI conversation context and monitor handoff triggers;
note right
  **Initial Entity State**
  BM01 Intended: ChatSession.status = **AI_ACTIVE**
  (DB Implementation: ChatSession.is_active = **True**)
end note

if (Which handoff trigger condition occurs?) then (DS-07: Guest explicitly requests human staff)
  |Hotel Guest|
  :Tap "Call Staff" button or ask voice assistant\nfor a human operator;
else (DS-08: Negative guest expression detected)
  |Concierge Robot|
  :Detect negative or frustrated guest expression\nduring interaction;
  note right
    **Design-to-Implementation Gap (DS-08)**
    BM01 specifies camera-based negative expression trigger.
    In baseline `review-2`, `guestEmotion` defaults to `'neutral'`
    and `concierge_graph.py` only sets `trigger_video_call=True`
    on explicit guest request/keyword (no active facial classifier).
  end note
endif

|Concierge Robot|
:Initiate human escalation process, create live call session,\nand log Concierge support request;
note right
  **Entity State Transition**
  BM01 Intended:
  • ChatSession.status: **AI_ACTIVE -> ESCALATED_HUMAN**
  • SupportRequest.status = **PENDING**
  (DB Implementation: HumanSupportSession.status = **"Active"**,
  SupportRequest.status = **"Pending"**)
end note

fork
  |Concierge Robot|
  :Display waiting/ringing video call modal to guest;
fork again
  |Front Desk Staff|
  :Receive real-time incoming call notification\nand audible ring alert on Concierge Dashboard;
end fork

|Front Desk Staff|
if (Front Desk Staff accepts incoming call before timeout?) then (No - Staff unavailable or call unanswered)
  |Concierge Robot|
  :Display staff unavailable / unanswered notification\nand preserve pending support request for follow-up;
  note right
    **Unanswered Call Handling (SRS 3.3.6 / DS-04c)**
    SupportRequest.status remains **PENDING** ("Pending")
    so Front Desk Staff can review and follow up.
  end note
  |Hotel Guest|
  :View unanswered message and close call modal;
  stop

else (Yes - Staff accepts call)
  |Front Desk Staff|
  :Accept video call and join WebRTC signaling room;

  |Concierge Robot|
  :Establish two-way WebRTC audio/video connection\nand start call session recording;

  repeat
    |Hotel Guest|
    :Speak in preferred language (e.g., English) during live call;

    |Concierge Robot|
    :Capture audio stream, perform STT transcription,\ntranslate EN <-> VN, and broadcast bilingual subtitles & TTS;

    |Front Desk Staff|
    :Read live translated subtitles and provide assistance\nin staff language (e.g., Vietnamese);
  repeat while (Two-way assisted communication continues?) is (Yes - Conversation active) not (No - Assistance completed)

  |Front Desk Staff|
  :End live video call session;

  |Concierge Robot|
  :Stop media tracks, upload call recording,\nand update session & support request states;
  note right
    **Entity State Transition**
    BM01 Intended:
    • SupportRequest.status: **PENDING -> RESOLVED**
    • ChatSession: **CLOSED**
    (DB Implementation: HumanSupportSession.status = **"Resolved"**
    with recording_url; SupportRequest.status = **"Completed"**;
    ChatSession.is_active = **False**)
  end note

  |Hotel Guest|
  :View call completion summary and return to main screen;
  stop
endif

@enduml

